speechtext:
Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-7. Meats, fresh, n.o.p.:
(a)	beef and veal, per pound: British preferential tariff, 4 cents; intermediate tariff, 6 cents; general tariff, 8 cents;
(b)	lamb and mutton, per pound: British preferential tariff, 4 cents; intermediate tariff, 6 cents; general tariff, 8 cents;
(c)	n.o.p., per pound: British preferential tariff, 2 cents; intermediate tariff, 2£ cents; general tariff, 5 cents.

Now I wish to point out
one or two matters to the Prime Minister. We in the maritime provinces are very much concerned about this duty, since we use a great deal of tin plate in the canning of fish.
22110-239}
